+barabar | 3rd century BCE | Barabar Caves | religion, technology, arts | gangetic | Barabar Caves | The Barabar caves | The Barabar Hill Caves in Bihar are the oldest surviving rock-cut caves in India. They date from the Maurya Empire, and some carry inscriptions of Ashoka, in the name of "King Piyadasi". | The oldest rooms carved out of solid rock in India are at Barabar in Bihar. They were made in the time of the emperor Ashoka.
