+lion-capital | 250 BCE | Dhamek Stupa | arts, power, religion | gangetic | Lion Capital of Ashoka | The Lion Capital at Sarnath | The Lion Capital of Ashoka is the head of a column erected by the Mauryan emperor Ashoka at Sarnath about 250 BCE. It is crowned by four life-sized lions set back to back. | About 250 BCE the emperor Ashoka set up a pillar at Sarnath with four stone lions on top. Today the lions are the emblem of India.
