+elephanta | 550 | Elephanta Caves | religion, arts | west | Elephanta Caves | The Elephanta caves | The Elephanta Caves, on an island in Mumbai's harbour, are a collection of cave temples mainly dedicated to the Hindu god Shiva. They are most commonly placed between the 5th and 7th centuries, and many scholars consider them complete by about 550 CE. | On an island near Mumbai are cave temples with giant carvings of the god Shiva.
